hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27763","Haddathana Yahya ibn Said from Sufyan from Mansur from Ribi from Tariq ibn Abd Allah al-Muharibi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you pray, do not spit to your right nor before you, and spit behind you and to your left if it is empty, and otherwise then thus, and that is under his foot; and Waki nor Abd al-Razzaq said: and spit behind you; and they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me."
"27764","Haddathana Muhammad ibn Jafar who said: Haddathana Shuba from Mansur who said: I heard Ribi ibn Hirash from Tariq ibn Abd Allah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When you pray, do not spit before you nor to your right, but spit toward your left if it is empty, and otherwise under your feet, and rub it."
"27765","Haddathana Ubayda ibn Humayd who said: Haddathani Mansur from Ribi ibn Hirash from Tariq ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not spit before you nor to your right, but from toward your left or under your foot, then rub it."
